y the anchor blockhouse, making the requested compound comparisons incomplete. T-3040 adds scene-aware `also_render` groups: every required member loads before capture, uses its dated scene phase and placement, and contributes its mesh and placement to the review fingerprint. Changed context or reference pixels invalidate an old verdict; missing or wrong-scene members fail explicitly.\n\nThe research checkpoint contains actual 30-member first-fort and 21-member second-fort comparisons plus findings from six reviewers across all 17 requested tickets. Both fort cameras remain provisional and both reviews say `differs`. T-3041 and T-2388 retain the original full matching acceptance; this PR does not close either model ticket or change geometry, placement, grade, or source-rights rulings. This support prerequisite is the named visible-progress exception for those fort comparisons.\n\nValidation:\n- Full reader-required preflight: 1,047 checks passed, exit 0; committed-diff changelog and ticket-ID checks also passed.\n- Published mobile smoke, stage 10: 31 passed, 0 failed.\n- Published desktop smoke, stage 3: 107 passed, 0 failed; 10m30s under CPU contention exceeded the documented 10-minute foreground budget. No assertion was weakened.\n- Group transform, asset/placement fingerprint and malformed-input tests, including the real image closing gate.\n- Both compound CLI renders inspected; unresolved differences preserved. Smoke scope is the tool-change recommended slices, not the entire renderer suite.\n\nRecovery checkpoint: https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets/tree/main/evidence/image-match-2026-10-22/t3040-compound-review-checkpoint\n\nIntegration refresh: updated head `7c1d95a801d18ba66f8ced83cb211bb0522f68d7` includes the latest integrated dev building-date change. Preserved both status entries; both fort group fingerprints are unchanged. Restored the known stale ignored Glessner light asset from the checked upstream package, then reran reader-required pref